{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1126329-attempting-to-understand-my-inner-mage","id":1126329,"title":"Attempting to understand my inner mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-08T09:11:37-07:00","id":1126329,"title":"Attempting to understand my inner mage","content":"So heres what I have so far,<br /> <br /> The character is based off of the chinese drunken fist/8 immortals/the drunken style. <br /> He had some really bad shite happen to him and his family during the Troubles and just left and started following this little man who took him drinking all over the world [later to be found out its his avatar] <br /> <br /> My question is if this actually works with rules as written for an Akashic Brotherhood member.<br /> Paradigm: Everything is Chaos, Your just not Drunk enough to understand.<br /> Practice: Through drinking and the use of ones own chi anything is possible you just have to pluck the right cord in the chaos. [While cord doesn't exactly fit, its the best that I can actually put to words.]<br /> Tools: He only starts with 2 Spheres Life and Entropy. Life is Chi [which must be moved via martial arts], and Entropy Drinking from his Gourd.[Not it must be his Gourd not some ramdom bottle]<br /> <br /> <br /> I have looked and read a bit, and I think this works, but I can't tell since i created it I am not sure I can be the most Objective","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11950-whatdoesitevenmatter","name":"Whatdoesitevenmatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T11:08:20-07:00","id":1126381,"title":"","content":"Well in order to have just Life and Entropy you'd have to take Life as his affinity Sphere and put a lot of freebie points to start with Arete 3. I'm assuming M20 since in previous editions the affinity Sphere of the Akashayana was Mind. Since that is the case you're going to need to select a minimum of 7 instruments. You have Food &amp; Drink, Cups &amp; Vessels, Energy (chi), and Martial Arts so far (that's my best guess based on what you've written). The gourd will be a unique instrument for you, but it would have to be for your affinity Sphere unless your ST allows otherwise. I recommend Thought Forms, Meditation, and possibly Weapons as additional instruments. Page 566 has a list you can draw from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","user":"PazuzuAxelf","date":".  Auto correct errors 08-08-2017, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T18:06:16-07:00","id":1126905,"title":"","content":"Any reason you have to be an Akashic? A drunken chi fighter could easily be a Chakravanti/Euthanatos, especially if they see themselves as an Agent of the Wheel. Entropy is the affinity sphere for most Chakravanti. Also, the Akashic Brotherhood is a tradition which highly emphasizes discipline and being a drunken master seems a more left-hand path philosophy.<br /> <br /> Though I'd suggest some Mind to go with the Life and Entropy. Mind 1 gives you mental strength and multitasking, so the drunken master can keep some mental faculties intact while drunk. At character generation, I'd go Arete 3 with Entropy 2, Life 3, Mind 1 and then decide if you want more kung fu or a rank of Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T21:35:00-07:00","id":1126954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1126329-attempting-to-understand-my-inner-mage?p=1126905#post1126905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reason you have to be an Akashic? A drunken chi fighter could easily be a Chakravanti/Euthanatos, especially if they see themselves as an Agent of the Wheel. Entropy is the affinity sphere for most Chakravanti. Also, the Akashic Brotherhood is a tradition which highly emphasizes discipline and being a drunken master seems a more left-hand path philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first of all, the Akashics have Left Hand Path followers of their own, specifically the Li-Hai.<br /> <br /> Second, if we're talking Left Hand, wouldn't the Cult of Ecstasy be just as appropriate, if not more so, as the Euthanatoi? Their's is a path all about the sacred excess, pursued to push the limits and achieve an altered state of mind. If anyone is going to imbibe their way to enlightenment, it's the Sahajiya.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T18:32:56-07:00","id":1127420,"title":"","content":"I was going with the chaotic master of death as the drunken master meme. I was thinking more of the death-dealing kung fu master but the Sahajiya could be pretty awesome. Normally Time is the Cult of Ectasy's specialty sphere but things can be different if a group wants them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T22:43:45-07:00","id":1127490,"title":"","content":"According to M20, the expanded list for the Cult of Ecstasy is Time, Life, and Mind. So the drunken master could easily focus Life. Or Mind, since we've suggested getting at least one dot. But probably Life, since it's more immediately in line with the character's strengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}